   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 219 of the laws of 2003, amending the education law\nrelating to publishers or manufacturers providing printed instructional\nmaterials for college students with disabilities, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7702",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7702-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 219 of 2003",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7702\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 219 of the laws of 2003, amending the education\nlaw relating to publishers or manufacturers providing printed instruc-\ntional materials for college students with disabilities, in relation to\nthe effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo purpose of this bill is to extend the law that provides college\nstudents with disabilities electronic formats of instructional materi-\nals.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill would amend chapter 219 of the laws of 2003 to\nextend the law for an additional three years through August 15, 2028.\n\nSection two of the bill would provide for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would ensure that students with disabilities have full access\nto instructional materials in suitable formats for use in colleges in\nNew York State by extending current law provisions for an additional\nthree years.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 283 of the Laws of 2022.\n\nChapter 171 of the Laws of 2019.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
